\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Study area and regional circulation around the South Shetland Islands, Antarctica. Circles mark the High-frequency Acoustic Recording Package (HARP) sites at Elephant Island (EI; 2014), King George Island (KGI; 2015--2016), and Clarence Island (CI; 2016), shown on GMRT bathymetry (v4.4.1; Ryan et al.~2009) with 500-m isobaths. Black arrows show mean surface currents for 2009--2021 from the Copernicus Marine Service global ocean physics reanalysis (GLORYS12V1). Black dashed and dot-dashed lines mark the Southern Antarctic Circumpolar Current Front (SACCF) and the Southern Boundary of the Antarctic Circumpolar Current (SB), respectively (Orsi et al.~1995). Colored lines show schematic pathways digitized from Damini et al.~(2025): intrusion of modified Circumpolar Deep Water (mCDW); the Bransfield Current (BC), carrying Transitional Zonal Water with Bellingshausen Sea influence (TBW), and its recirculation; the Antarctic Coastal Current (ACoC), carrying Transitional Zonal Water with Weddell Sea influence (TWW); the Antarctic Slope Front (ASF) and associated eddy; and the Peninsula Front (PenF). The inset shows the location of the study area (red box) relative to the Antarctic Peninsula and South America.}}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-map}{{1}{4}{Study area and regional circulation around the South Shetland Islands, Antarctica. Circles mark the High-frequency Acoustic Recording Package (HARP) sites at Elephant Island (EI; 2014), King George Island (KGI; 2015--2016), and Clarence Island (CI; 2016), shown on GMRT bathymetry (v4.4.1; Ryan et al.~2009) with 500-m isobaths. Black arrows show mean surface currents for 2009--2021 from the Copernicus Marine Service global ocean physics reanalysis (GLORYS12V1). Black dashed and dot-dashed lines mark the Southern Antarctic Circumpolar Current Front (SACCF) and the Southern Boundary of the Antarctic Circumpolar Current (SB), respectively (Orsi et al.~1995). Colored lines show schematic pathways digitized from Damini et al.~(2025): intrusion of modified Circumpolar Deep Water (mCDW); the Bransfield Current (BC), carrying Transitional Zonal Water with Bellingshausen Sea influence (TBW), and its recirculation; the Antarctic Coastal Current (ACoC), carrying Transitional Zonal Water with Weddell Sea influence (TWW); the Antarctic Slope Front (ASF) and associated eddy; and the Peninsula Front (PenF). The inset shows the location of the study area (red box) relative to the Antarctic Peninsula and South America}{figure.caption.3}{}}
