\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces Effect of duty cycling on odontocete detections, estimated by subsampling the continuous recordings at Clarence Island (CI) to the duty cycles used at Elephant Island (EI; 5 min on every 6 min) and King George Island (KGI; 10 min on every 13.33 min) at 100 random phase offsets. Panels show the percentage of detection events, positive 5-min bins, and presence days retained relative to continuous recording. Points show the mean and bars the range across phase offsets. Dashed horizontal lines mark the proportion of time recorded under each duty cycle (83.3\% for EI, 75.0\% for KGI). Open symbols mark species not detected at the site whose duty cycle was simulated (sperm whale at KGI). BW58 is not shown because it was not detected at CI. Pm, sperm whale; Gm, long-finned pilot whale; Oo, killer whale; BW29, southern bottlenose whale; BW37, BW37 beaked whale.}}{21}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-duty}{{S3}{21}{Effect of duty cycling on odontocete detections, estimated by subsampling the continuous recordings at Clarence Island (CI) to the duty cycles used at Elephant Island (EI; 5 min on every 6 min) and King George Island (KGI; 10 min on every 13.33 min) at 100 random phase offsets. Panels show the percentage of detection events, positive 5-min bins, and presence days retained relative to continuous recording. Points show the mean and bars the range across phase offsets. Dashed horizontal lines mark the proportion of time recorded under each duty cycle (83.3\% for EI, 75.0\% for KGI). Open symbols mark species not detected at the site whose duty cycle was simulated (sperm whale at KGI). BW58 is not shown because it was not detected at CI. Pm, sperm whale; Gm, long-finned pilot whale; Oo, killer whale; BW29, southern bottlenose whale; BW37, BW37 beaked whale}{figure.caption.15}{}}
